--TEST--
A `fill` that asks `getSecret` for the key it is filling is a `LogicError` rather than a wait on itself, and the hold it took is released whichever way the call ended — `rule:concurrency/a-secret-fill-runs-once-per-process`
--FILE--
<?nvs
secret bytes $key = Core\Crypto::generateKey();
array<secret bytes> $ring = [$key];

var $store = Core\Cache::process();

// The one caller filling a key holds it for as long as its `fill` runs, so a
// `fill` asking for that same key is asking to wait for itself. It is told so
// where the mistake is, rather than at the end of a bound it would spend
// first.
var $selfAsking = fn (): Core\Cache\SecretEntry => {
    var $inner = fn (): Core\Cache\SecretEntry => Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of("inner", 1h);
    var $asked = $store->getSecret("self-asking", $ring, {fill: $inner});
    return Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of("outer", 1h);
};
try {
    $store->getSecret("self-asking", $ring, {fill: $selfAsking});
    echo "the fill answered", "\n";
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo "a fill asking for its own key is a logic error", "\n";
}

// The fill never answered, so nothing was stored: what a `fill` throws is the
// caller's own failure and no entry at all, rather than a value some other
// request would inherit.
echo "and nothing was stored: ", $store->getSecret("self-asking", $ring) == null ? "null" : "something", "\n";

// The hold is released whichever way the call ended, so the next caller runs
// its own `fill` rather than finding the key wedged for the life of the
// process.
var $later = fn (): Core\Cache\SecretEntry => Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of("later", 1h);
var $after = $store->getSecret("self-asking", $ring, {fill: $later});
echo "the key is left to the next caller: ", ($after ?? "") == "later" ? "yes" : "no", "\n";
--EXPECT--
a fill asking for its own key is a logic error
and nothing was stored: null
the key is left to the next caller: yes
